{"agent":"main","body":{"args_hash":"sha256:73995356d62def74144ae93a6e481db2d610177a11954938574884c4536e788e","args_inline":{"content":"---\nname: project-money-cents\ndescription: pricing/money.py Money class stores integer cents internally, not a float dollar amount\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`Money` in `pricing/money.py` was refactored from a float-backed `dataclass(frozen=True)` to a hand-written class storing `cents: int` internally (via `__slots__` + `__setattr__` override for immutability). The public constructor still takes a dollar float (`Money(0.10)`) and rounds to the nearest cent; `.amount` is now a read-only property (`cents / 100`) kept for backward compatibility with `pricing/tax.py`, `pricing/format.py`, and `pricing/report.py`.\n\n**Why:** float amounts drifted (three 0.10 widgets summed to 0.30000000000000004), breaking equality checks and finance CSV totals.\n\n**How to apply:** any new arithmetic on Money should operate on `.cents` (use `Money.from_cents(...)`) rather than on `.amount`, to avoid reintroducing float drift. `pricing/report.py`'s CSV row formatting was changed to `f\"{...:.2f}\"` since `.amount` alone no longer produces trailing zeros once drift is gone.\n","file_path":"/var/folders/yb/b_617z_s2ml933nmr_k7m47m0000gn/T/saga-bench-448289159/py-0008-money-exact-cents/1/cfg/claude-config/projects/-private-var-folders-yb-b-617z-s2ml933nmr-k7m47m0000gn-T-saga-bench-448289159-py-0008-money-exact-cents-1-ws/memory/project_money_cents.md"},"component":"harness","cwd_rel":".","index_version":null,"tool":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q54Faij8eomzan8EzXhHkS"},"hash":"sha256:276b6102b87bb273d6437ef609543c5053e880a6acd68aef18705296a1c2b6b1","mono_ns":39000000,"prev":"sha256:c607eb94bddd89d68e67c5cfdec16c16398e91c6f7e350e3c6c78a603a420b2f","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":39,"session":"bf71126b-5f42-4d90-9b9b-121ebb3e16b6","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.039Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_call"}
